Package: ssh3-client
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: ssh3-c maintainers <maintainers@example.com>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, ssh3c-libssl3 | ssh3-server (>= 0.4.0-1)
Conflicts: ssh3-go-client
Replaces: ssh3-go-client
Description: SSH3 client - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 transport
 The SSH3 client: sessions, the ssh(1)-canon forwards (-L/-R/-D with
 the udp:// extension), -J proxy jumps, the control master (-M/-S/-O),
 the agent forwarding (-A), file transfers (put|get, -r recursive) and
 the in-process sftp subsystem, all over one HTTP/3 (QUIC) extended
 CONNECT per target.
 .
 The CLI follows the ssh(1) canon: -4/-6, -e escape, -F ssh_config,
 -o keyword overrides, -t/-T pty control, -V.  The first connection
 pins the server certificate TOFU-style in ~/.ssh3/known_hosts.
 The OpenSSL 3.5 QUIC TLS API rides the bundled private libraries of
 ssh3c-libssl3 (the RUNPATH pins /usr/lib/ssh3-c/lib), so any system
 libssl is fine.  See ssh3(1).
